From: Luke Johnson <jaewun@me.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: panel-chipone-icna35xx: do not fail disable on DCS error

icna35xx_disable() hands dsi_ctx.accum_err straight back to the DRM
core.  A failed DCS transfer therefore turns into a failed ->disable,
and drm_panel_disable() only clears drm_panel::enabled on success:

	if (panel->funcs && panel->funcs->disable) {
		ret = panel->funcs->disable(panel);
		if (ret < 0)
			goto exit;
	}
	panel->enabled = false;

The next drm_panel_enable() then short-circuits:

	if (panel->enabled) {
		dev_warn(panel->dev, "Skipping enable of already enabled panel\n");
		return;
	}

This panel has no ->enable callback, so the flag being wrong costs
exactly one thing: the backlight_enable() below that early return is
never reached.  A display that otherwise came back cleanly stays black,
and because drm_panel_disable() stops at the same goto exit, every
subsequent recovery attempt starts from the same wrong state.

Observed on AYN Thor while recovering a stalled DSI-2 link: the
garbled-panel recovery sends DCS SET_DISPLAY_OFF, that transfer times
out (-110; dsi_cmd_dma_tx() waits 200 ms for CMD_MDP_DONE at
dsi_host.c:1458), and the very next enable logs "Skipping enable of
already enabled panel" -- so each failed recovery leaves the next one
starting from a worse place.

Log the error and report success.  The panel is powered down in
icna35xx_unprepare() regardless of what the DCS said, and there is no
action a caller could take on this error anyway: the only recovery is
a full re-prepare, which is what the next enable or modeset does.

Kept local to this driver rather than teaching the generic
drm_panel_disable() to clear ->enabled on a partially failed disable,
since other panels can fail for reasons where the flag does matter.

Tested by inspection and by 'git apply --check' against the synced
ROCKNIX SM8550 tree.  No AYN Thor hardware was available, so the
behavioural claim comes from the device journal, not a before/after
run.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-chipone-icna35xx.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-chipone-icna35xx.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-chipone-icna35xx.c
@@ -346,7 +346,21 @@
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_enter_sleep_mode_multi(&dsi_ctx);
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(&dsi_ctx, 120);
 
-	return dsi_ctx.accum_err;
+	/*
+	 * Do not propagate a failed DCS transfer.  drm_panel_disable()
+	 * only clears drm_panel::enabled when ->disable succeeds, so
+	 * returning accum_err here leaves the core believing the panel is
+	 * still on.  The next drm_panel_enable() then early-returns with
+	 * "Skipping enable of already enabled panel" and never reaches
+	 * backlight_enable(), so a display that did come back stays black.
+	 * There is no ->enable here for it to skip, so that flag is the
+	 * only thing the failure costs us, and unprepare() powers the
+	 * panel down regardless of what the DCS said.
+	 */
+	if (dsi_ctx.accum_err)
+		dev_warn(panel->dev, "DCS disable failed: %d\n", dsi_ctx.accum_err);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int icna35xx_unprepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
